# NFL Roster Transaction Timing & Prop-Market Adjustment Lags
*Research Agent 17 deliverable. Sources: NFL Football Operations, ESPN, Action Network,
Tech Insider, OddsIndex, Rotowire, NFL Contract Language. Compiled from live web research.*

All 2024+ CBA rules apply to the **2026 season** (cut-down day is a single date; 17-player
practice squads; IR returns after 4 games; no per-season DTR cap — see notes).

---

## 1. 2026 TRANSACTION CALENDAR (key dates, all ET) — source: NFL Football Operations

| Date | Deadline / window | What moves |
|---|---|---|
| **Aug 30** | **6:00 PM** | 53-man roster cutdown. Single cutdown date (since 2024 CBA). PUP/NFI players simultaneously: place on Reserve/PUP or Reserve/NFI **or** terminate/trade/waive/fail-physical. |
| **Aug 30 (business day)** | cutdown day | Teams may designate for return **max 2** players placed on a Reserve List this business day (these count against the 8 regular-season IR return slots). |
| **Aug 31** | 1:00 PM | Waiver claims from cut-down expire. Clubs may **establish practice squad (17 players; 1 Intl Pathway; ≤6 vets, 10 rookies/2nd-years)**. |
| **Sep 6** | end | Training camp ends for all clubs. |
| **Oct 2 day-after 4th game & Oct 5–6** | 4:00 PM | Earliest a player on Reserve/PUP or Reserve/NFI may be **activated** (must have served minimum 4 games). |
| **Nov 10** | **4:00 PM** | **Trade deadline — all trading ends for 2026.** |
| **Nov 11** | — | Players with ≥4 accrued seasons become subject to **waiver system** for remainder of season. |
| **Weekly (reg. season)** | Wed / Fri 4PM / Sat | Injury reports; **Inactives** announced Fri–Sat for Sunday games. Thu/Fri reports for Wed games. |

> Note on date drift: cut-down day was Tue Aug 26 (2024/25), Sun Aug 30 (2026). It is **always
> late August, 6:00 PM ET**, always a single cut-down date. The trade deadline is **always Week 9
> Tuesday**, 4:00 PM ET (Nov 4 in 2025 → Nov 10 in 2026).

---

## 2. TRANSACTION TYPES & THEIR MECHANICS (the timing rules you trade against)

### CUTS (53-man reduction) — Aug 30, 6:00 PM ET
- Teams carry 90 in camp; must submit final 53 to the league by the deadline.
- **Process lag**: transactions are submitted electronically → processed via a league
  *Personnel Notice*; the binding roster is the one at 6:00 PM. Teams tip moves in the 24–48 h
  before the deadline ("cut-down Thursday/Friday" news cycle), but **rosters aren't final until
  the stroke of 6 PM** — so depth-chart / snap-share assumptions can be stale for ~1 day.
- Waiver claims run Aug 31, 1:00 PM (claims processed overnight; claiming priority by draft order
  through Week 3, then by current standings). → **claims aren't resolved until the next calendar
  day**, so who actually sticks on a roster isn't known until Aug 31 afternoon.
- Practice squad is set Aug 31 onward — final 53 + practice-squad picture solid by Aug 31 1 PM.

### TRADES
- **In-season**: any time except the Nov 10 (4 PM) deadline. A deal can be agreed/leaked **before**
  the deadline and still collapse, or be reported **after** the fact — settlement risk window.
- **Off-season**: trading period opens **March 11, 4:00 PM ET** (after all contracts expire that
  league year).
- **Post-deadline processing**: Nov 11 onward, transactions are published in a daily batch
  *Personnel Notice* covering ~4:00–10:00 PM ET (the "portal" window). → a trade agreed at 6 PM
  on a Tuesday may not be *official* until the next morning's notice cycle.

### INJURED RESERVE (IR) PLACEMENT + RETURN
- **During final cut-down (Aug 30)**: teams may place up to 2 players on IR and designate them for
  return simultaneously; those 2 count against the season's return slots.
- **During the season**: any player can be placed on IR mid-season.
- **Return rule (since 2022 CBA)**: a player placed on IR must miss a **minimum of 4 games**
  before being designated for return; there is **no longer a 2-DTR cap** — but each team has
  **up to 8 return activations per season** (source: ESPN / NFL). Per player, max 2 returns.
- **Activation window**: once designated for return, the player has **21 days** to be moved to
  the active roster; must clear physical/progressively ramping practice.
- **Edge**: the *moment* a player is ruled out for the season (IR placement) → market reacts in
  seconds on the primary prop, but the *return timeline* and "next man up" role props lag.

### PUP / NFI
- Placed at cut-down (Aug 30) simultaneously with 53-man reduction.
- **Activation window**: may not return until after serving **minimum 4 games**
  (eligible Oct 2 day-after / Oct 5–6, 4 PM ET). → a player on PUP is **out for Weeks 1–4**,
  a known fixed window that markets price early but role-benefit to backups lags.

### PRACTICE SQUAD → ACTIVE ROSTER (Elevations / Call-ups)
- **Standard Elevation Addendum**: a team may elevate **up to 2 practice-squad players per game**;
  each player can be elevated **max 3 times per season** before the team must sign them to the
  53 (4th elevation = roster move + waivers). (Source: NFL contract language / ESPN)
- Elevations are typically submitted **Friday–Saturday** for a Sunday game (or Saturday for a
  Monday game); processed via the league notice cycle. → the elevated player's snap-count prop
  may not appear or be adjusted for **hours** after elevation.
- Practice squad = **17 players** (2025+), incl. 1 International Pathway slot.

---

## 3. REPORTING / PROCESSING SPEED (the "wire lag")

| Step | Speed |
|---|---|
| Team announces via official X/social account → | **seconds** |
| Sportsbook auto "circles" game (odds-scrape for "out / torn / indefinitely") | **seconds to ~2 min** |
| Primary player prop + spread + total re-price | **minutes (≈2–10 min)** |
| Secondary / "next-man-up" teammate props re-price | **hours (often 2–12 h unsteady)** |
| League *Personnel Notice* (officially binds move) | next daily batch (**4–10 PM ET portal** window, or overnight for cut-down claims) |
| Waiver claims resolve (cut-down) | **next calendar day** (Aug 31, 1 PM ET deadline → results overnight) |

> The market reacts far faster than the league's official processing. A player can be *ruled
> out* on a team's social feed at 9 AM and the books reprice in minutes, while the league
> notice that formally places him on IR / terminates the contract may not drop until the
> evening batch.

---

## 4. WEEKLY PROP-MARKET CYCLE (the windows you trade against)
*Sources: Tech Insider "NFL Betting Guide", Action Network, BetrQL day-by-day, Rotowire.*

| Period | Market state | Edge / risk |
|---|---|---|
| **Mon–Tue** | Next week's props **open**. Opener carries largest hold, lowest limits. | Early value if model sees a number; lines volatile. |
| **Wed** | Injury Report #1 (practice participation). | Base-game line near peak efficiency; **prop boards widest** here. |
| **Wed close** | Line at ~peak "sharp" efficiency (Mon–Wed = sharp-money window). | Cleanest baseline; retail money hasn't flowed yet. |
| **Thu–Fri** | Retail money flows in; **final injury report due Fri 4 PM ET** for Sunday games. | Line drifts on public money; **biggest prop mis-pricing window** as role changes aren't fully priced. |
| **Fri–Sat** | **Inactives** announced for Sunday games (league requires submission ~10 AM ET Sunday; teams tip Fri/Sat). | Primary prop adjusts in minutes; secondary/teammate props lag **hours** — core edge window. |
| **≤4 h pre-kickoff** | Largest line movements of the week on news flow. | Props begin locking; some books pull markets on breaking news. |
| **10–30 min pre-kickoff** | Props lock (varies by book; spread/total often locked earlier). | Late inactives can't be bet, but earlier role-bets may settle. |

---

## 5. THE EDGE WINDOWS (transaction → prop lag) — the deliverable

### EDGE WINDOW A — "Seconds" circle, "Hours" to stabilize (headline news)
- When credible injury/transaction news hits, books **circle** the game within seconds and
  reopen minutes later with primary player + spread + total re-priced (often over-adjusted,
  then reined in by sharp money during "price discovery").
- Source: Action Network — *"the gap between 'news' and 'market adjustment' is measured in
  **seconds**, not minutes"*; books scrape social/news for "out/torn/indefinitely."

### EDGE WINDOW B — Secondary/"next man up" props lag **HOURS**  *(biggest, most reliable edge)*
- *"A player's prop line might not move for **hours** after news breaks that a key teammate is
  out, even though that absence directly affects the player's expected [output]."* — OddsIndex.
- When a starter is ruled out → his backup's snap/share/role **doesn't fully reprice for 2–12 h**.
- Action Network: target the **Over** on the secondary option's usage/share prop right after the
  primary goes down, before the book adjusts the secondary line.

### EDGE WINDOW C — Cut-down week (Aug 28–31) fixed-window lag
- Rosters final Wed night/Thu (6 PM Aug 30); waiver claims + practice squads settle the
  **next calendar day** (Aug 31). Teams' depth-chart/SnapShare decisions made at **6:00 PM Aug 30**
  → weekly props (Week 1+) may price before that picture is locked → **~24 h stale role props**.
- Best exploited: week-before-next week's snap-count / target-share props on players whose
  roster fate was only sealed at the Aug 30 deadline.

### EDGE WINDOW D — Practice-squad elevation lag (Fri–Sat → Sunday)
- Elevations submitted Fri–Sat don't fully reprice the elevated player's snap-count prop or the
  displaced incumbent's prop for **hours** after elevation is processed.
- Each player max **3 elevations/season**; 2 elevations **per game** — so a team cycling
  rookies creates recurring weekly mis-pricings.

### EDGE WINDOW D2 — PUP/NFI fixed absence (Weeks 1–4)
- Player on PUP at cut-down = **out Weeks 1–4**, activation eligible only Oct 5 (4 PM).
  Markets price the long absence early; the beneficiary role props adjust slowly.

### EDGE WINDOW E — Trade deadline (Nov 10, 4 PM) settlement gap
- Trades agreed/leaked before 4 PM can collapse; trades reported after the deadline may
  already be priced. Books may remove markets on breaking trade news and reopen with **reduced
  limits** → thin-liquidity edge window (sharps first in).

### EDGE WINDOW F — IR-return timeline vs. activation window
- IR placement → market reacts instantly. But **return** is gated: min 4 games missed, then 21-day
  window to activate. The *value* of the returning player's prop vs. the incumbent who's been
  playing is mis-priced until the **designation-for-return** moment (the 21-day countdown window).

---

## 6. KEY CAVEAT — NFL prop-market clampdown (2025–2026)
- The NFL has issued **memos to teams limiting prop-bet info** shared with betting partners and is
  working with state regulators to restrict certain player props (esp. around injury/news timing).
  Books increasingly **pull markets preemptively** on breaking transaction news and reopen with
  reduced limits, which *shortens* some edge windows and widens the bid-ask spread.
- Source: NYT Athletic (Nov 2025), ESPN.

